diff --git a/README.md b/README.md
index 19ac5351..021305e2 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -111,6 +111,8 @@ Remote monitoring is opt-in. Configure an SSH host alias in `~/.ssh/config` for
 logs, including its user, port and identity as needed. Use normal SSH host-key verification, pre-trust the host key,
 and use noninteractive key or SSH agent authentication. Enable each host in Settings → Sources. Local sources and all
 enabled remote sources appear together in the native dashboard; source identity includes the host and source kind.
+Settings → Sources shows each host's online, offline or disabled status and its last connection error until a successful
+snapshot arrives.
 Local diagnostic reports and live reporting contain local data only, not remote data. Remote SSH is independent of the
 network switch: disable the host to stop it. The app selects its bundled collector for the host architecture, uploads
 it over SSH and runs it over SSH standard streams. There is no HTTP service, listening port, Python runtime or sudo.
@@ -119,6 +121,7 @@ The Linux collector reuses the native measurement core, including omp parsing an
 remote host has its own identity and history, separate from local usage. A disconnected host is shown offline with
 stale data, not as idle or zero usage; reconnection replaces its snapshot and history rather than adding them again.
 On macOS, cached history remains stale after reconnecting until a new history frame arrives, even if live snapshots resume.
+When multiple connections report the same machine, history is selected per source; stale or partial status reflects every connection whose history contributes.
 Fields absent from logs are unknown. Live rates inferred from recent completed responses are estimates; completed
 response rates use the logged duration. In particular omp commonly writes a response when it completes, so remote
 monitoring cannot measure per-token streaming speed or infer an unrecorded time to first token. End-to-end speed includes
